@notes-done-flag-api
Feature: Notes Done-Flag API
  As a signed-in note owner
  I want to set a note's done flag through the API
  So that I can mark my notes complete or incomplete without leaving the application

  Background:
    Given I am signed in as a user with a valid bearer token
    And I own a note with id "note-1" whose done flag is false

  # Why: FEAT-PO-001 — the core capability the request names: the owner flips the done flag and gets the updated note back
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] A successful update returns HTTP 200 with the updated note as the JSON response body
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Owner sets a note's done flag to true
    When I send PATCH /api/notes/note-1 with a JSON body containing done set to true
    Then the request should succeed
    And the response should return the updated note with id "note-1" and done set to true
    And all other attributes of the note should remain unchanged

  # Why: FEAT-PO-001 — the request names both directions of the toggle, so the false direction is its own key example
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Owner sets a note's done flag to false
    Given I own a note with id "note-2" whose done flag is true
    When I send PATCH /api/notes/note-2 with a JSON body containing done set to false
    Then the request should succeed
    And the response should return the updated note with id "note-2" and done set to false
    And all other attributes of the note should remain unchanged

  # Why: FEAT-PO-001 — the input states the update is idempotent, so re-sending the same value must be stable
  @key-example
  Scenario: Re-sending the same done value yields the same updated note
    When I send PATCH /api/notes/note-1 with a JSON body containing done set to true
    And I send PATCH /api/notes/note-1 with a JSON body containing done set to true again
    Then the request should succeed
    And the response should return the updated note with id "note-1" and done set to true

  # Why: FEAT-PO-001 — the done flag accepts only boolean true/false, so both accepted values are exercised at the boundary of the accepted set
